      "writtenOn": "2017-12-06T15:48:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m actually not sure what\u0027s the best thing to do if they don\u0027t match:\n1) Reject the transaction (don\u0027t support nested transactions for nodes with a dedicated thread)\n2) Use passed-in thread - keeps binder semantics but violates \"node thread\" semantics\n3) Use node thread - violates binder semantics, and requires fixing up t-\u003eto_thread, maybe more nastiness.\n\nAlso the reverse case - if a transaction passed through a node with dedicated thread, and it makes a transaction to the same process, it would be handled by the node thread, even if the node it makes a call on doesn\u0027t have a dedicated thread assigned.",
      "parentUuid": "2c6b33e0_b94ebbdf",
      "revId": "c5c82efc2ca13ba882fe1e5e0e3ac10d68f4f80f",
